  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Saving Lives &amp; Building Resilience by Bridging the Gap between Humanitarian Assistance and Development in Bogot&#xE1; and Santander, Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As of August 2023, Migraci&#xF3;n Colombia reports approximately 2.89 million Venezuelan migrants in Colombia under the Temporary Status of Protection. These migrants face vulnerabilities due to various factors. The Inter-Agency Group on Mixed Migration Flows forecasts over 402,000 in-transit migrants, 1.9 million people in pendular movement, and around 980,000 Colombian returnees. This situation creates a demand for humanitarian assistance and integration processes across Colombia. Aligned with the Colombian Government&apos;s priorities, this project aims to support the Regional Refugee and Migrant Response Plan, addressing the needs of refugees, migrants, Colombian returnees and host communities affected by mixed migration flows. This twelve-month project aims to bridge humanitarian and development assistance by supporting shelter, enhancing healthcare access, protecting victims of trafficking and promoting economic integration in Bogot&#xE1; and Santader.</narrative>
  </description>
